WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.272
This simple record illustrates representation cleaning.

00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:06.302
The name changes spacing and display case.

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:11.072
The email is trimmed and lowercased.

00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:13.592
The phone keeps only digits.

00:00:13.592 --> 00:00:19.572
Each transformation is explainable. But the cleaned value should not erase the source evidence.

00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:22.647
In many analytical workflows, raw and cleaned layers are both valuable.

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:30.117
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:35.997
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.997 --> 00:00:43.702
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.702 --> 00:00:49.387
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:55.287
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
